/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:3:// Minimal dict support. A dict value is `dictV(KS, VS)`: PARALLEL insertion-ordered key/value
/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:4:// ValSeqs (Python dict order; keys distinct; re-inserting a key updates its value in place, keeping
/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:5:// the original position). Concrete for krun (the ordered build + `.keys()` are the real ops); a proof
/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-6-// over a SYMBOLIC dict passes `dictV(KS, WS)` with a symbolic key sequence KS and reads
/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-7-// `d.keys() = list(KS)`, then keeps each key opaque problem-locally.
/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-8-//
